Maybe I'm biased by playing primarily conjurers (who tend to have access to
something unresistable to fling at enemies), but I've never really had a
problem with the outcomes of /oPO when not testing under stress. The one time
when I was in effect killed by zap-testing a /oPO was the exception that
proves the rule -- I was low on at least three of the following: HP, MP,
healing and food, and I converted a heavily damaged yak into, I think, a
slime creature that I just could, not, shake, and I eventually made a misstep
and died.

(Actually, I think there's a bug in the code for the wands' effects, as the
result tends to be the same thing an awful lot of the time -- a human on the
early dungeon levels, an elf a little later on. Hmmm... For a conjurer, the
humans are nice, since they give good experience, while being neither speedy
nor able to attack at a distance nor especially hard to kill.)

